{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "37449751-31a8-5ead-9525-88759fdfd1b0"/*VolumeShakingWaterExample*/,
  "Description": "The container is an open box: a box minus a slightly smaller box with [VolumeCsg] Difference. The water is a slab displaced by [VolumeNoise] and clipped by Intersection to the inside of the box. Two [OscillateVec3] make the box shake and the water slosh.\n\nAKA: water, liquid, slosh, container, csg, noise, animation\n\nTips\n- Smaller VoxelSize means sharper surfaces and more memory and time; start coarse and refine.\n- Level sets store signed distance in world units (negative inside); fog volumes store density.",
